{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"custom-languages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Languages"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A language definition maps source ranges to the library's semantic token classes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"minimal-definition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minimal definition"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createHighlighter,\n  defineLanguage,\n  type TokenRange,\n} from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\n\nconst taskList = defineLanguage({\n  name: 'task-list',\n  aliases: ['tasks'],\n  tokenize(code) {\n    const ranges: Array<TokenRange> = []\n    const pattern = /\\b(?:TODO|DONE|BLOCKED)\\b/g\n    let match: RegExpExecArray | null\n\n    while ((match = pattern.exec(code))) {\n      ranges.push({\n        start: match.index,\n        end: match.index + match[0].length,\n        className: match[0] === 'DONE' ? 'inserted' : 'keyword',\n      })\n    }\n\n    return ranges\n  },\n})\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [taskList],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineLanguage()"},{"type":"text","value":" is an identity helper that preserves the literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"range-contract","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Range contract"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TokenRange"},{"type":"text","value":" contains:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type TokenRange = {\n  start: number\n  end: number\n  className: HighlightTokenClass\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ranges use zero-based, end-exclusive UTF-16 offsets. Return non-overlapping\nranges. The core clamps and sorts ranges by source position, then drops invalid\nor overlapping entries before creating tokens. A broad range that starts first\ncan therefore suppress a more specific range inside it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefer leaving text unclassified over assigning an inaccurate class. Gaps are preserved as plain text automatically."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"delegation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Delegation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tokenizer receives a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TokenizerContext"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type TokenizerContext = {\n  hasLanguage(lang: string): boolean\n  tokenize(code: string, lang: string): Array<TokenRange>\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An outer definition can delegate a substring and offset the returned ranges into its own source coordinates. Check "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasLanguage()"},{"type":"text","value":" first so the dependency remains optional."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avoid making a custom definition import another shipped definition directly. Registry delegation preserves selective imports and lets the application decide dependencies."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"semantic-classes-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic classes only"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom definitions must use an existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HighlightTokenClass"},{"type":"text","value":". This keeps themes complete and prevents language-specific CSS scope proliferation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"contribution-bar","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Contribution bar"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new shipped language should have:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A real documentation use case"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An isolated module"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common valid-code fixtures"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source reconstruction coverage"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focused tests for any context-aware scanner"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Acceptable impact only when explicitly imported"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A language requiring a general grammar runtime is not a fit for this package."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"custom-languages","text":"Custom Languages","level":1},{"id":"minimal-definition","text":"Minimal definition","level":2},{"id":"range-contract","text":"Range contract","level":2},{"id":"delegation","text":"Delegation","level":2},{"id":"semantic-classes-only","text":"Semantic classes only","level":2},{"id":"contribution-bar","text":"Contribution bar","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Custom Languages\n\nA language definition maps source ranges to the library's semantic token classes.\n\n## Minimal definition\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createHighlighter,\n  defineLanguage,\n  type TokenRange,\n} from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\n\nconst taskList = defineLanguage({\n  name: 'task-list',\n  aliases: ['tasks'],\n  tokenize(code) {\n    const ranges: Array<TokenRange> = []\n    const pattern = /\\b(?:TODO|DONE|BLOCKED)\\b/g\n    let match: RegExpExecArray | null\n\n    while ((match = pattern.exec(code))) {\n      ranges.push({\n        start: match.index,\n        end: match.index + match[0].length,\n        className: match[0] === 'DONE' ? 'inserted' : 'keyword',\n      })\n    }\n\n    return ranges\n  },\n})\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [taskList],\n})\n```\n\n`defineLanguage()` is an identity helper that preserves the literal `name` type.\n\n## Range contract\n\nEach `TokenRange` contains:\n\n```ts\ntype TokenRange = {\n  start: number\n  end: number\n  className: HighlightTokenClass\n}\n```\n\nRanges use zero-based, end-exclusive UTF-16 offsets. Return non-overlapping\nranges. The core clamps and sorts ranges by source position, then drops invalid\nor overlapping entries before creating tokens. A broad range that starts first\ncan therefore suppress a more specific range inside it.\n\nPrefer leaving text unclassified over assigning an inaccurate class. Gaps are preserved as plain text automatically.\n\n## Delegation\n\nThe tokenizer receives a `TokenizerContext`:\n\n```ts\ntype TokenizerContext = {\n  hasLanguage(lang: string): boolean\n  tokenize(code: string, lang: string): Array<TokenRange>\n}\n```\n\nAn outer definition can delegate a substring and offset the returned ranges into its own source coordinates. Check `hasLanguage()` first so the dependency remains optional.\n\nAvoid making a custom definition import another shipped definition directly. Registry delegation preserves selective imports and lets the application decide dependencies.\n\n## Semantic classes only\n\nCustom definitions must use an existing `HighlightTokenClass`. This keeps themes complete and prevents language-specific CSS scope proliferation.\n\n## Contribution bar\n\nA new shipped language should have:\n\n- A real documentation use case\n- An isolated module\n- Common valid-code fixtures\n- Source reconstruction coverage\n- Focused tests for any context-aware scanner\n- Acceptable impact only when explicitly imported\n\nA language requiring a general grammar runtime is not a fit for this package.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Custom Languages\n---\n\n# Custom Languages\n\nA language definition maps source ranges to the library's semantic token classes.\n\n## Minimal definition\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createHighlighter,\n  defineLanguage,\n  type TokenRange,\n} from '@tanstack/highlight/core'\n\nconst taskList = defineLanguage({\n  name: 'task-list',\n  aliases: ['tasks'],\n  tokenize(code) {\n    const ranges: Array<TokenRange> = []\n    const pattern = /\\b(?:TODO|DONE|BLOCKED)\\b/g\n    let match: RegExpExecArray | null\n\n    while ((match = pattern.exec(code))) {\n      ranges.push({\n        start: match.index,\n        end: match.index + match[0].length,\n        className: match[0] === 'DONE' ? 'inserted' : 'keyword',\n      })\n    }\n\n    return ranges\n  },\n})\n\nconst highlighter = createHighlighter({\n  languages: [taskList],\n})\n```\n\n`defineLanguage()` is an identity helper that preserves the literal `name` type.\n\n## Range contract\n\nEach `TokenRange` contains:\n\n```ts\ntype TokenRange = {\n  start: number\n  end: number\n  className: HighlightTokenClass\n}\n```\n\nRanges use zero-based, end-exclusive UTF-16 offsets. Return non-overlapping\nranges. The core clamps and sorts ranges by source position, then drops invalid\nor overlapping entries before creating tokens. A broad range that starts first\ncan therefore suppress a more specific range inside it.\n\nPrefer leaving text unclassified over assigning an inaccurate class. Gaps are preserved as plain text automatically.\n\n## Delegation\n\nThe tokenizer receives a `TokenizerContext`:\n\n```ts\ntype TokenizerContext = {\n  hasLanguage(lang: string): boolean\n  tokenize(code: string, lang: string): Array<TokenRange>\n}\n```\n\nAn outer definition can delegate a substring and offset the returned ranges into its own source coordinates. Check `hasLanguage()` first so the dependency remains optional.\n\nAvoid making a custom definition import another shipped definition directly. Registry delegation preserves selective imports and lets the application decide dependencies.\n\n## Semantic classes only\n\nCustom definitions must use an existing `HighlightTokenClass`. This keeps themes complete and prevents language-specific CSS scope proliferation.\n\n## Contribution bar\n\nA new shipped language should have:\n\n- A real documentation use case\n- An isolated module\n- Common valid-code fixtures\n- Source reconstruction coverage\n- Focused tests for any context-aware scanner\n- Acceptable impact only when explicitly imported\n\nA language requiring a general grammar runtime is not a fit for this package.\n"}
